-- Clos.seg: what each declaration's informal text opens.
-- Notation (opened to expose the shape of a type, "A x", a pair, Id Bool _ true):
--   Cl Iff Cap Sub Eqv tau M scA OTc Tr Tr3 LT TT OK NZ isZero isA isR isI Lex SP KmP C4
--   NFsum NFsum' NFphi NFom NFpsi QQ Sums, and this file's packages and their parts
--   (WD WDs WDp WDo WDk DC DSum DCard DR WU WUs WUp WUo WU0 UC USum UPhi UOm UUp Ini H415
--   Pre AddC UpH UpQ FQ BS PsiP G1 G2 G3 PhiC PhiD Bnd Bar Seg SH WDC).
-- WA, Bar, Seg, tau, scA (4.12, 4.5) where the text applies them; le where it says "y <=' x: y <' x or y = x".
-- cat also in sums-split (Sums of cat x y), bs-plus, bs, ca-sums; one, isZero (1 /= 0), suc in lt-suc-self, km-C-om;
-- omF in omF-z (Omega_0 = 0); kminus in lt-km-psi, lt-km, ok-km, km-C (I^- = 0, Omega'_e^- = Omega_{pred e}).
-- Computational definitions, opened where the text says "by definition":
--   cat ((x0, xs) y = (x0, cat xs y), g y = (g, y)) in cat-lt-l, cat-lt-r, pre-P, add-cat-P, suc-cat;
--   add (Def. 2.10(a)) in add-zero, add-cat; phiF (2.10(c)) in u-phi; suc = _ + 1 in suc-up, hd-suc, fq-R;
--   card, up, tilde, mFi, cardS, hd, kminus, omF (Defs. 2.13(a), (b)) in the clause-by-clause
--   proofs u-up, u-up-psi, d-tilde, fq, fq-psi, fq-R, R-in, d-R, dR-om, card-psi-*; mI (2.13(c)) in d-mI.
-- Closed computations: ok-zero, ok-ii, ok-one, mfi-one, nfphi-one, up-zero (isOT, lt, card, ...).
-- card-phi (refl) also opens le/lt/cmp2/fwd/or: unfolding card at phi evaluates its Boolean
-- le x1 x0 (a checker artefact, as CA's cin-psi); its uses open none of them.
